1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,690
Meet CoachMe — AI coaching for racket sports.

2
00:00:04,150 --> 00:00:11,461
CoachMe turns a practice video into actionable coaching: what to fix, the exact moment it happened, and the drill to fix it.

3
00:00:12,090 --> 00:00:14,586
The player on the left is Michael, from our team.

4
00:00:14,586 --> 00:00:20,442
This is his table-tennis backhand topspin drill — ten seconds, one camera, no sensors.

5
00:00:22,070 --> 00:00:25,341
Before the model writes anything, CoachMe measures the clip.

6
00:00:25,341 --> 00:00:31,105
It samples the moments where motion happens, tracks the player and the ball, and maps movement over time.

7
00:00:32,690 --> 00:00:38,276
These are the exact frames the vision model reads — not the whole video, just the moments that matter.

8
00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:42,167
The Analysis tab keeps the measurements separate from the coaching.

9
00:00:42,167 --> 00:00:48,452
Movement shows where the action happened; Pose shows the body as a skeleton, with joint angles frame by frame.

10
00:00:50,030 --> 00:00:57,491
At the bottom of the Pose tab, Body 3D turns that skeleton into a model you can rotate, with the measured joint angles for the frame.

11
00:00:58,280 --> 00:01:01,574
Then every finding carries a timestamp and a confidence.

12
00:01:01,574 --> 00:01:10,799
Here's the key one: the elbow drops below wrist level during the backswing — high confidence — at 1.5, 3.1 and 7.0 seconds.

13
00:01:10,799 --> 00:01:12,269
Let's look at 1.5.

14
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:17,136
Michael didn't notice this until the report showed him.

15
00:01:17,136 --> 00:01:20,758
The elbow drop is real — and he can check it because it's his clip.

16
00:01:23,630 --> 00:01:30,096
The report connects that to the result: with the elbow low, the paddle closes, so the swing goes forward instead of up.

17
00:01:30,096 --> 00:01:32,827
That's why the arc is flat and there's no topspin.

18
00:01:32,827 --> 00:01:38,475
It also credits what's working: a compact, repeatable stroke, contact in front of the body.

19
00:01:40,130 --> 00:01:47,626
Then it turns the diagnosis into practice: shadow backhand loops with the elbow at waist height, brushing up, finishing at chin height.

20
00:01:47,626 --> 00:01:48,934
One click marks it done.

21
00:01:51,640 --> 00:01:53,951
Measure, coach, drill, track.

22
00:01:53,951 --> 00:01:59,263
Table tennis is just the start — badminton, squash, padel and tennis are next.

23
00:01:59,263 --> 00:02:00,201
That's CoachMe.
